  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "First run fetches weights, a status read never does",
      "items": [
        "Weights are 622 MB, CC-BY-4.0, and land in the app's own userData directory: four files whose sizes are checked on every read, never vendored into the repository.",
        "voiceStatus answers from disk before asking the engine to warm up, so mounting a composer cannot start a 622 MB download (engine.ts, model.ts:184).",
        "A fresh install enables the mic and reports needs-download; the first click fetches with progress shown, and the click after it records (session.ts:146).",
        "prepare is its own call, so an interrupted fetch leaves the next click free to retry rather than stranding the engine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Interruption rules",
      "items": [
        "A tap under 300 ms is discarded rather than transcribed, and capture keeps a pre-roll so the first syllable is not clipped (capture.ts:15).",
        "Accepted work is never cancelled by a later utterance and output keeps submission order; a late result for a cancelled or superseded capture cannot reach the composer (controller.ts:29).",
        "Decodes are serialized behind one queue: overlapping calls into a single ONNX session are unsafe.",
        "Recording is cut into 35 s windows before inference, which is a reference-processor window rather than an encoder limit (chunk.ts:20)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Measured on this machine, not assumed",
      "items": [
        "A 7.4 s clip decodes in about 350 ms with punctuation and casing restored; two threads beat both one and four, and memory plateaus after warm-up.",
        "The short-audio guard sits at 400 samples, five times the measured cliff below which the native addon aborts the process instead of throwing.",
        "Both guards fire in JavaScript before the addon sees a buffer or a path, because neither failure is catchable."
      ]
    }
  ]
